### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5090

# ==============================================================================
# SECTION 1: DEFAULT API CONTRACT ENDPOINTS (/api/...)
# Adheres strictly to ASSIGNMENT.md table
# ==============================================================================

### 1.1 Create room (expected: 201 Created with Location header)
# @name createRoomDefault
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Study room 1",
  "capacity": 10
}

###
@defaultRoomId = {{createRoomDefault.response.body.$.id}}

### 1.2 Get room (expected: 200 OK)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{defaultRoomId}}

### 1.3 Get a missing room (expected: 404 Not Found)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001

### 1.4 Create booking (expected: 201 Created with Location header)
# @name createBookingDefault
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{defaultRoomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "ana",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-10T10:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-10T12:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 4
}

###
@defaultBookingId = {{createBookingDefault.response.body.$.id}}

### 1.5 Get booking (expected: 200 OK)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{defaultBookingId}}

### 1.6 Overlapping booking - Rule R7 (expected: 409 Conflict)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{defaultRoomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "bogdan",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-10T11:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-10T13:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 4
}

### 1.7 Touching booking - Rule R7: touching intervals do NOT overlap (expected: 201 Created)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{defaultRoomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "clara",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-10T12:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-10T14:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 4
}

### 1.8 Cancel booking - Rule R8 (expected: 204 No Content)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{defaultBookingId}}/cancel

### 1.9 Cancel already cancelled booking - Rule R8 (expected: 409 Conflict)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{defaultBookingId}}/cancel

### 1.10 Cancel missing booking - Rule R8 (expected: 404 Not Found)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/cancel


# ==============================================================================
# SECTION 2: BUSINESS RULES VALIDATION (R1 - R6)
# ==============================================================================

### 2.1 R1: Room name is empty (expected: 400 Bad Request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "capacity": 10
}

### 2.2 R1: Capacity is non-positive (expected: 400 Bad Request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Invalid Room",
  "capacity": 0
}

### 2.3 Room does not exist -> 404 returned before any validation (expected: 404 Not Found)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "",
  "startUtc": "2020-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2020-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "attendees": -1
}

### 2.4 R2: bookedBy is missing/empty (expected: 400 Bad Request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{defaultRoomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "   ",
  "startUtc": "2030-02-10T10:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-02-10T12:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 2
}

### 2.5 R3: endUtc is before/equal to startUtc (expected: 400 Bad Request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{defaultRoomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "dan",
  "startUtc": "2030-02-10T12:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-02-10T10:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 2
}

### 2.6 R4: attendees <= 0 (expected: 400 Bad Request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{defaultRoomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "dan",
  "startUtc": "2030-02-10T10:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-02-10T12:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 0
}

### 2.7 R4: attendees exceeds room capacity (expected: 400 Bad Request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{defaultRoomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "dan",
  "startUtc": "2030-02-10T10:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-02-10T12:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 999
}

### 2.8 R5: booking starts in the past via TimeProvider (expected: 400 Bad Request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{defaultRoomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "dan",
  "startUtc": "2020-01-01T10:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2020-01-01T12:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 2
}

### 2.9 R6: duration exceeds 4 hours for capacity <= 10 (expected: 400 Bad Request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{defaultRoomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "dan",
  "startUtc": "2030-02-10T10:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-02-10T14:01:00Z",
  "attendees": 2
}

### 2.10 R6: exactly 4 hours is allowed for capacity <= 10 (expected: 201 Created)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{defaultRoomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "dan",
  "startUtc": "2030-02-10T10:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-02-10T14:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 2
}


# ==============================================================================
# SECTION 3: VERSION 1 ENDPOINTS (/api/v1/...)
# Explicit versioning with /v1 prefix
# ==============================================================================

### 3.1 v1 - Create room (expected: 201 Created)
# @name createRoomV1
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/rooms
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Quiet Lab v1",
  "capacity": 6
}

###
@roomV1Id = {{createRoomV1.response.body.$.id}}

### 3.2 v1 - Get room (expected: 200 OK)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/rooms/{{roomV1Id}}

### 3.3 v1 - Create booking (expected: 201 Created)
# @name createBookingV1
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/rooms/{{roomV1Id}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "elena",
  "startUtc": "2030-03-01T09:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-03-01T11:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 3
}

###
@bookingV1Id = {{createBookingV1.response.body.$.id}}

### 3.4 v1 - Get booking (expected: 200 OK)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/bookings/{{bookingV1Id}}

### 3.5 v1 - Cancel booking (expected: 204 No Content)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/bookings/{{bookingV1Id}}/cancel


# ==============================================================================
# SECTION 4: VERSION 2 ENDPOINTS (/api/v2/...)
# Enhanced RESTful conventions, sub-resources, and HTTP verbs
# ==============================================================================

### 4.1 v2 - Create room (expected: 201 Created)
# @name createRoomV2
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/rooms
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Innovation Hub v2",
  "capacity": 15
}

###
@roomV2Id = {{createRoomV2.response.body.$.id}}

### 4.2 v2 - Get room by ID (expected: 200 OK)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/rooms/{{roomV2Id}}

### 4.3 v2 - Create booking for room (capacity > 10, max 2 hours => 201 Created)
# @name createBookingV2
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/rooms/{{roomV2Id}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "felix",
  "startUtc": "2030-04-01T14:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-04-01T16:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 8
}

###
@bookingV2Id = {{createBookingV2.response.body.$.id}}

### 4.4 v2 - RESTful Sub-resource: List active bookings for room (expected: 200 with 1 booking)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/rooms/{{roomV2Id}}/bookings

### 4.5 v2 - Get booking by ID (expected: 200 OK)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/bookings/{{bookingV2Id}}

### 4.6 v2 - RESTful DELETE: Cancel booking using standard HTTP DELETE (expected: 204 No Content)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/bookings/{{bookingV2Id}}

### 4.7 v2 - Verify active bookings is now empty after cancellation (expected: 200 with empty array [])
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/rooms/{{roomV2Id}}/bookings

### 4.8 v2 - RPC-style POST cancel is also supported for backward compatibility (expected: 409 already cancelled)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/bookings/{{bookingV2Id}}/cancel


# ==============================================================================
# SECTION 5: NEW REQUIREMENTS (R9, R10, R11)
# ==============================================================================

### 5.1 Create rooms for R9 and R10 testing
# @name roomSmall
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Small Lab (Capacity 8)",
  "capacity": 8
}

###
@smallRoomId = {{roomSmall.response.body.$.id}}

### 5.2 Create large room for R10 testing (capacity > 10)
# @name roomLarge
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Conference Hall (Capacity 20)",
  "capacity": 20
}

###
@largeRoomId = {{roomLarge.response.body.$.id}}

### 5.3 R10: Capacity > 10 booked for > 2 hours (expected: 400 Bad Request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{largeRoomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "tester1",
  "startUtc": "2030-05-10T10:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-05-10T12:01:00Z",
  "attendees": 15
}

### 5.4 R10: Capacity > 10 booked for exactly 2 hours (expected: 201 Created)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{largeRoomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "tester1",
  "startUtc": "2030-05-10T10:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-05-10T12:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 15
}

### 5.5 R9: Participant Booking 1 on 2030-06-01 (expected: 201 Created)
# @name r9Booking1
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{smallRoomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "participantA",
  "startUtc": "2030-06-01T08:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-06-01T10:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 4
}

###
@r9Booking1Id = {{r9Booking1.response.body.$.id}}

### 5.6 R9: Participant Booking 2 on same day in different room (expected: 201 Created)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{largeRoomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "participantA",
  "startUtc": "2030-06-01T11:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-06-01T13:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 12
}

### 5.7 R9: Participant Booking 3 on same day across all rooms (expected: 409 Conflict)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{smallRoomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "participantA",
  "startUtc": "2030-06-01T14:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-06-01T16:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 4
}

### 5.8 R9: Participant Booking on a different day (expected: 201 Created)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{smallRoomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "participantA",
  "startUtc": "2030-06-02T08:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-06-02T10:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 4
}

### 5.9 R9: Cancel Booking 1 to free a daily slot (expected: 204 No Content)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{r9Booking1Id}}/cancel

### 5.10 R9: Third booking now succeeds because cancelled bookings do not count (expected: 201 Created)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{smallRoomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "participantA",
  "startUtc": "2030-06-01T14:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-06-01T16:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 4
}

### 5.11 R11: Cancel booking with < 60 minutes before start (expected: 409 Conflict)
# Note: In real testing, use a booking starting in < 60 minutes from current UTC time.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/cancel
